[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m // wrapper is under test too.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m // `driver` reports its result on stdout via `printf(3)`, so "compare the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m // outputs" means: redirect fd 1 to a temp file, call one library, flush the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m // shared libc stdout buffer, and read the bytes back. Comparison is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m // byte-for-byte.
